Calculator Program Using Methods

Write a Java program to design a Calculator that performs basic arithmetic operations. 
Create four separate methods: add(), subtract(), multiply(), and divide(). 
Accept two numbers from the user at runtime, pass them as parameters to the respective methods, 
return the calculated result from each method, and display the output on the console.

Requirements:
Create four methods:
add(int a, int b)
subtract(int a, int b)
multiply(int a, int b)
divide(int a, int b)
1.Accept input values from the user at runtime.
2.Pass the input values as arguments to the methods.
3.Each method should return the calculated result.
4.Print the returned result in the main method.

public class Calculator {

    // Addition Method
    public static int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }

    // Subtraction Method
    public static int subtract(int a, int b) {
        return a - b;
    }

    // Multiplication Method
    public static int multiply(int a, int b) {
        return a * b;
    }

    // Division Method
    public static double divide(int a, int b) {

        if (b == 0) {
            System.out.println("Division by zero is not allowed.");
            return 0;
        }

        return (double) a / b;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter First Number: ");
        int num1 = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.print("Enter Second Number: ");
        int num2 = sc.nextInt();

        int addition = add(num1, num2);
        int subtraction = subtract(num1, num2);
        int multiplication = multiply(num1, num2);
        double division = divide(num1, num2);

        System.out.println("\n===== Calculator Result =====");
        System.out.println("Addition       : " + addition);
        System.out.println("Subtraction    : " + subtraction);
        System.out.println("Multiplication : " + multiplication);
        System.out.println("Division       : " + division);

            }
}


